    <bpmn:process id="W_W4789" name="W4789. Uptime/SLA Management, Availability Reporting &amp; Penalty Administration" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Continuous SLA monitoring; monthly CPO review; SLA breach
Frequency: Continuous + monthly
Volume: 1 network SLA across all ~205 sites (uptime target ≥ 97%)
Owner: EV Program Manager / IT (VS-27)
Participants: CPO (W4770), IT (VS-27), Finance (VS-17), Legal (VS-100.3)
Source: workflow W4789 — Uptime/SLA Management, Availability Reporting &amp; Penalty Administration</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4789_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4789_Lane1" name="IT">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4789_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4789_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4789_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W4789_Lane2" name="EV Program">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4789_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4789_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4789_Start4" name="Continuous SLA monitoring; monthly CPO review; SLA breach">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4789_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4789_Task5" name="Monitor uptime/SLA per the CPO contract (W4770) and internal targets…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Monitor uptime/SLA per the CPO contract (W4770) and internal targets: per-charger and network availability, session-success rate, time-to-repair (W4786), and fault frequency; track against the SLA thresholds (e.g., 97–99% availability) via the CSMS (W4781)
Responsible (R): IT / EV Program
Accountable (A): EV Program Manager
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4789_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4789_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4789_Task6" name="Administer SLA penalties/credits and vendor governance: where the CPO…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Administer SLA penalties/credits and vendor governance: where the CPO underperforms, apply contractual credits/penalties (W4770), manage performance improvement plans, and escalate persistent underperformance to re-compete (W4770); reconcile with Finance
Responsible (R): EV Program / Finance / Legal
Accountable (A): EV Program Manager / Legal
Duration: Monthly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4789_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4789_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4789_Task7" name="Report availability to internal stakeholders (store ops, leadership) and…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Report availability to internal stakeholders (store ops, leadership) and publish charger availability to drivers (app VS-75 / roaming W4782) so drivers see live status; feed uptime performance to analytics (W4792) and the network-strategy review (W4769)
Responsible (R): IT / EV Program / App team
Accountable (A): EV Program Manager
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4789_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4789_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4789_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4789_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-140 (ensure EV-charging uptime &amp; tariff compliance.) | - CTL-721: uptime monitored vs SLA; penalties/credits administered; live availability published; performance feeds strategy
Owner: EV Program Manager / IT (VS-27)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
